    <!-- The sound driver runs on the 68000: the game's vertical-blank interrupt calls it once a frame (0x71B4C), it plays the songs
         and effects and writes the YM2612 and the PSG itself. The Z80 only plays the sampled sounds (drums, the SEGA chime). The Machine
         runs the 68000 for just that: it calls the game's routine that loads the Z80's program and starts the driver (0x134C), then the
         driver's routine at every vertical-blank interrupt. The request for a song or an effect is a byte of the 68000's RAM (0xFFF00B)
         that the driver takes at its next frame. 0x81-0x93 are songs, 0xA0-0xCF effects, 0xE1 the SEGA chime (a sampled sound), 0xE4 stops
         everything. The game does not say the region it was sold in (JUE): the console is the Japanese one (Mega Drive, 60 Hz). -->
    <driver m68k_init="0x134C" m68k_frame="0x71B4C" request="0xFFF00B" warmup_frames="4" region="japan" cart_crc32="afe05eee"/>
